# Code Standards

These standards apply to ALL code in this project.

## Language & Style

- Use [TypeScript/JavaScript] with strict mode enabled
- Follow [ESLint/Prettier] configuration in the project
- Prefer [async/await] over callbacks
- Use [named exports] over default exports

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | kebab-case | `user-service.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `UserService` |
| Functions | camelCase | `getUserById` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| Interfaces | PascalCase with I prefix (optional) | `IUserRepository` or `UserRepository` |

## File Organization

```
src/
+-- api/           # API routes/controllers
+-- services/      # Business logic
+-- models/        # Data models/entities
+-- repositories/  # Data access layer
+-- middleware/     # Express/framework middleware
+-- utils/         # Shared utilities
+-- types/         # TypeScript type definitions
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
// Use custom error classes
class NotFoundError extends Error {
  constructor(resource: string) {
    super(`${resource} not found`);
    this.name = 'NotFoundError';
  }
}

// Always catch and handle appropriately
try {
  const user = await userService.getById(id);
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof NotFoundError) {
    return res.status(404).json({ error: error.message });
  }
  throw error; // Re-throw unexpected errors
}
```

### Error Response Format

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "User not found",
    "details": {}
  }
}
```
